{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Abraham said, etc. — O that Ishmael, etc.</b> He intends in this prayer that Ishmael walk in righteousness before HaShem, and this is the meaning of <b>may he live before You</b> — for the righteous are called 'alive.' And his saying <b>before You</b> follows the verse's saying ״וְאַתֶּם הַדְּבֵקִים בַה׳״ etc. (Deuteronomy 4:11), and he needed to pray because he saw in him signs that were not good — for in any case the wickedness of the wicked is not hidden from the eyes of the righteous, and all the more so in the case of his own son; therefore he prayed for him that he be righteous, and he disclosed his thinking that this was his desired one, as I explained in the verse (Genesis 15:3) ״הֵן לִי״. And HaShem had promised him that his seed would be like the stars, and he asks that this promise be fulfilled in Ishmael."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:38.784106433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}